===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[clean]] and [[jerk]]}}

# {{lb|en|weightlifting}} The act of lifting the [[barbell]] from the floor to a resting position across the front of the shoulders (the clean phase), [[pause|pausing]], and [[thrust]]ing the barbell over the head to a [[stationary]] position in one movement (the jerk phase).  The normal technique for both parts of this act involves propelling the barbell upwards, quickly lowering the torso, and then straightening the legs.

